cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use any of the datasets curated here, please cite BOTH the original
  dataset (or its paper) AND the corrected release you actually used — they are
  not identical, so a citation to the original alone does not describe the data.
title: "KeenForgeData — curated niche vision datasets"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "KeenForgeAI"
    website: "https://huggingface.co/KeenForgeAI"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KeenForgeAI/KeenForgeData"
url: "https://github.com/KeenForgeAI/KeenForgeData"
repository-artifact: "https://huggingface.co/KeenForgeAI"
abstract: >-
  A curated collection of high-quality niche computer-vision datasets, published
  openly on Hugging Face and ModelScope. Public niche datasets are frequently
  noisy — loose boxes, missed objects, mislabels, duplicated images, inconsistent
  class names. KeenForgeAI re-annotates and cleans them with KeenForge, documents
  every change, and releases them with full provenance and citations.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - object detection
  - niche datasets
  - industrial inspection
  - medical imaging
  - annotation quality
  - dataset curation
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-20"

references:
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      GC10-DET-corrected: a cleaned release of the GC10-DET steel surface defect
      dataset
    authors:
      - name: "KeenForgeAI"
    year: 2026
    version: "1.0"
    publisher:
      name: "KeenForgeAI"
    doi: "10.57967/hf/10526"
    notes: >-
      Derived from Lv et al. (2020), doi:10.3390/s20061562. Upstream licence
      unstated. Curated by Lu Gan and Sam Li.

  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      TXL-PBC-corrected: a corrected release of the TXL-PBC peripheral blood cell
      dataset
    authors:
